- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/compareblend.html
- Summary (EN): Compare and Blend works per pixel. It compares input A against input B and selects pixels from either the true or the false input, so the result blends between two sources. The page calls it a pixel switcher based on specific values. Available since Houdini 22.0.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Compare and Blend choisit pixel par pixel entre deux sources selon la comparaison de A et B, ce qui en fait un aiguillage entre deux couches.

- Inputs meaning: ["true: source for pixels where the comparison passes", "false: source for pixels where it fails", "A: value being compared", "B: value compared against A", "tolerance (optional): mono per-pixel tolerance"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer, VDB or attribute", "True If: equal, not equal, A greater than B, A greater than or equal to B, A less than B, A less than or equal to B", "B Value: fallback constant for B when B is not wired", "Bias: shifts the result toward the true or false input (calculation not documented)", "Tolerance: band around the threshold, both sides for equality, one side for strict inequality", "Falloff: None, Linear, or Elendt (smooth S-curve)"]

- Caveats: ["The inequality labels are easy to misread (page lists B greater than A as (<)); check the operator against the description when wiring", "The page does not say how the tolerance input interacts with the Tolerance parameter; test before relying on it", "Not the separate Compare VOP node"]

